            "detailed_description": "SPACEPLAN is an experimental piece of interaction based partly on a total misunderstanding of Stephen Hawking’s A Brief History of Time. Use manual clicks and the passage of time to create and launch potato-based devices and probes from your nondescript satellite orbiting a mysterious planet. Unlock the mysteries of the galaxy or just kill some time in what the astrophysics community is calling the ‘best narrative sci-fi clicker game of all times’.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ></h2><li>Fifteen starchy items to unlock, create, and blast into the vacuum of space.<br></li><li>Life affirming, silly story that will both captivate and help you kill time.<br></li><li>Reveal the secrets of five different planets across two different realities.<br></li><li>Banging soundtrack, as is customary in a narrative sci-fi clicker game.</li></ul>",
            "about_the_game": "SPACEPLAN is an experimental piece of interaction based partly on a total misunderstanding of Stephen Hawking’s A Brief History of Time. Use manual clicks and the passage of time to create and launch potato-based devices and probes from your nondescript satellite orbiting a mysterious planet. Unlock the mysteries of the galaxy or just kill some time in what the astrophysics community is calling the ‘best narrative sci-fi clicker game of all times’.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ></h2><li>Fifteen starchy items to unlock, create, and blast into the vacuum of space.<br></li><li>Life affirming, silly story that will both captivate and help you kill time.<br></li><li>Reveal the secrets of five different planets across two different realities.<br></li><li>Banging soundtrack, as is customary in a narrative sci-fi clicker game.</li></ul>",
